;; sukashi 透かし — seed graph of the AD-TECH SUPPLY CHAIN + delivery infra + fraud networks
;; ADR-2606071600 · vocabulary: ad-supply-chain-ontology.kotoba.edn (00-contracts/schemas/)
;;
;; SCOPE: a bounded illustrative slice of the programmatic advertising ecosystem as a kotoba EAVT
;;   knowledge graph — the AD-TECH entities (DSP/exchange/SSP/ad-network/publisher/verification),
;;   the first-class AUTHORIZATION edges from the PUBLIC ads.txt / sellers.json web-standard files,
;;   ad CREATIVES (who broadcasts what), the DELIVERY edges binding a creative to its serving
;;   infrastructure (IP/ASN/WHOIS-org, reusing ip-network + passive-dns ontologies), and FRAUD
;;   SIGNALS. The lens is FRAUD PROTECTION + ad-tech TRANSPARENCY. NOT a target-list, NOT an ad
;;   network (sukashi G2). sukashi does NOT adjudicate (G4) — signals are routed, never verdicts.
;;
;; SOURCING (G5): real ad-tech firms + their genuinely-public ads.txt/sellers.json facts are
;;   :authoritative/:representative and carry NO fraud signal (non-adjudication; we do not impute
;;   wrongdoing to real companies). Every FRAUD example is attached to a CLEARLY-FICTIONAL entity
;;   (obviously-fake names + RFC-2606 .example / .test domains + RFC-5737 documentation IP ranges
;;   192.0.2.0/24, 198.51.100.0/24, 203.0.113.0/24) and is :synthesized. Delivery infra for
;;   illustrative cases uses documentation ranges so no real host is implicated. Absence of an
;;   entity = "not yet ingested", never "legitimate" or "does not exist". Full-web ads.txt /
;;   sellers.json / WHOIS crawl is G7 Council+operator gated.

